{
  "schema": "cdeadmin.ui-form.v1",
  "engine": "mysql",
  "family": "table",
  "resource_kinds": [
    "table"
  ],
  "form_reference": "SR-F-020057",
  "status": "complete",
  "engine_tab_title": "MySQL",
  "omitted_tabs": [],
  "gaps": [
    {
      "concept": "Separate column length/precision/scale/unsigned/identity/charset/collation/generated/comment controls",
      "reason": "The column record compiler consumes only name, type, nullable, default, unique and primary_key. Other native clauses currently require the full type declaration, not the drafted standalone field ids.",
      "tracking": "INV-MYSQL"
    },
    {
      "concept": "Partitions editor",
      "reason": "partition_by and add_partitions are operation ids with partition_clause/definitions/count drafts, not nested properties accepted by table.create. Decision 4 defaults to the Partitions tab; the typed operation-to-grid integration remains open.",
      "tracking": "INV-MYSQL"
    },
    {
      "concept": "ALTER grid diff and online algorithm/lock",
      "reason": "The current alter compiler accepts add_columns/drop_columns/rename_columns; it does not accept create-grid columns or alter_algorithm/alter_lock. The existing controlled-change workflow is separate. 2026-11-05: the Columns grid now adds, drops and renames columns in alter mode (the shared diff), and table options alter through ALTER TABLE. An existing column's type, nullability, default, uniqueness and key membership show locked on reopen: MODIFY COLUMN restates the whole column, and the grid does not carry every attribute to restate (character set, collation, generation, comment, visibility). ALGORITHM/LOCK remain unsurfaced.",
      "tracking": "INV-MYSQL"
    },
    {
      "concept": "Object privileges grid application",
      "reason": "privilege.grant is an operation address, not a table.create draft property. Cross-operation diff dispatch needs the shared shell contract.",
      "tracking": "INV-MYSQL"
    },
    {
      "concept": "MERGE member selection",
      "reason": "mysql_table_options.union accepts arrays of identifier-path arrays, not selected reference strings or grid records. Decision 9 records the missing value projection.",
      "tracking": "INV-MYSQL"
    },
    {
      "concept": "SECONDARY_ENGINE explicit NULL and JSON-attribute scalar variants",
      "reason": "The backend accepts None for SECONDARY_ENGINE and arbitrary JSON for engine attributes. This draft exposes named text and key/value objects only; the schema has no explicit nullable/text or nested typed JSON value projection.",
      "tracking": "INV-MYSQL"
    },
    {
      "concept": "Primary engine attributes outside beta profile",
      "reason": "Core SQL hooks require HTON_SUPPORTS_ENGINE_ATTRIBUTE. No implementation in the audited MySQL9.7 Community engine sources advertises it; release InnoDB/MyISAM/MEMORY reject index use with native error3981. Debug simulation is not product support. A separately available implementation and native qualification are required before surfacing this field. Secondary-engine attribute metadata is separate.",
      "tracking": "MY-POST-BETA-PRIMARY-ENGINE-ATTRIBUTES"
    },
    {
      "concept": "Constraint edits after create",
      "reason": "2026-11-05: constraint grids pre-fill on reopen and show locked. Adding, dropping and enforcing a constraint on an existing table are the constraint's own operations (create, drop, enforcement); the grids do not dispatch them."
    },
    {
      "concept": "Options that do not pre-fill",
      "reason": "2026-11-05: INSERT_METHOD, FEDERATED CONNECTION and engine attributes are not reported in a structured catalog column and do not pre-fill; ENCRYPTION pre-fills only when the table reports it (an unencrypted table shows no value). TEMPORARY, DATA DIRECTORY and INDEX DIRECTORY are create-only: ALTER TABLE ignores the directories."
    }
  ],
  "notes": "Typed create bindings include retained temporary tables, native FK actions and CHECK enforcement. Unsupported property projections stay in gaps. Canonical read-only tabs and SQL come from the shared shell; draft is not presentation acceptance. 2026-11-05: reopens and edits a table. Pre-fill from the inventory: table options from information_schema.TABLES (ENGINE, collation and its character set, comment, CREATE_OPTIONS) and SHOW CREATE TABLE (AUTO_INCREMENT, TABLESPACE, AUTOEXTEND_SIZE); columns from their catalog facts (type with AUTO_INCREMENT, default as SQL); constraints with key columns, references, actions and check expressions. Alter: the Columns grid adds, drops and renames columns; options compile to one ALTER TABLE (mysql_family/administration.py). The foreign-key grid cells are named as the compiler reads them (references_table, references_columns): the shell does not map a grid cell's backend_field_id, so foreign keys could not be created from this form before. Round-tripped against MySQL 9.7.0 (tools/tests/test_ui_descriptor_roundtrip_mysql.py).",
